S2DEX sprites through the 2D matrix are drawn (warecomp STATUS.md rounds 19 and 20).

G_OBJ_MOVEMEM (gSPObjMatrix, gSPObjSubMatrix) wasn't handled, and
G_OBJ_SPRITE / G_OBJ_LDTX_SPRITE / G_OBJ_LDTX_RECT_R loaded their texture
and drew nothing (TODOs). Worms Armageddon draws its rotating sprites that
way (func_8000762C: a rotation matrix, then G_OBJ_LDTX_SPRITE), among them
the air strike's target cursor, which didn't show at all.

The matrix is kept; a matrix sprite's corners go through it and it is drawn
as two textured triangles (RDP::drawTris), turned and scaled as the
microcode draws it; a RECTANGLE_R through the matrix's translation and base
scale. (The first version drew matrix sprites upright: the air strike's
target showed but didn't turn, round 20.)

